<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">295 events on the 31 days of October, from 4004 BCE to 2012: the best known of them, the people born and died in the month, its festivals and its songs.</p></header>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="mon-ev"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="mon-ev">The best-known events of October</h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-1"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/darius-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander defeats Darius III at Gaugamela</span><span class="tp">1 October 331 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-1"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/congress-of-vienna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">The Congress of Vienna is due to open formally</span><span class="tp">1 October 1814</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-2"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Julius Caesar arrives in Egypt and learns of Pompey's death</span><span class="tp">2 October 48 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-2"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mahatma-gandhi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mohandas Gandhi is born in Porbandar</span><span class="tp">2 October 1869</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-3"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Lincoln proclaims a national day of Thanksgiving</span><span class="tp">3 October 1863</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-5"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">The Beatles release their first single, 'Love Me Do'</span><span class="tp">5 October 1962</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-7"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">The epoch of the Hebrew calendar</span><span class="tp">7 October 3761 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-8"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/che-guevara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Che Guevara is captured in Bolivia</span><span class="tp">8 October 1967</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-11"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-leo-x.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Leo X names Henry VIII 'Defender of the Faith'</span><span class="tp">11 October 1521</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-11"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Roosevelt receives Einstein's warning about atomic bombs</span><span class="tp">11 October 1939</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-12"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Columbus makes landfall in the Bahamas</span><span class="tp">12 October 1492</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-15"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-of-flanders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Latin emperor Henry of Flanders defeats Theodore I Laskaris</span><span class="tp">15 October 1211</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-15"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Napoleon arrives in exile at Saint Helena</span><span class="tp">15 October 1815</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-16"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-leipzig.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">The Battle of Leipzig begins</span><span class="tp">16 October 1813</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-17"><span class="ph ph-event" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">The Queen opens Calder Hall nuclear power station</span><span class="tp">17 October 1956</s